{"text": "CASTELLANO & BRIGHT LLP -- TRUST ADMINISTRATION FILE NOTES\nMatter: Halvorsen Family Revocable Trust u/a/d June 3, 2009\nFile no. TR-2026-0318      Atty: Renee Castellano   Paralegal: Dmitri Volkov\n\n4/22/2026 (RC) -- Intake call with successor trustee Ingrid Halvorsen-Pike,\nthe settlor's eldest daughter. Settlor Arvid T. Halvorsen died\nFebruary 9, 2026 at Mercy Ridge Hospice in Duluth; he was age 94.\nHis wife Birgit predeceased him (d. 11/30/2019). Ingrid has the original\ntrust and the pour-over will. She does not have a death certificate yet; ordered six.\nMr. Halvorsen's SSN per the old 1040 is 250-96-2697. Trust has been using his\nSSN; need a new EIN now that it is irrevocable. Explained the Form 1041 filing and\nthat a Form 706 is unlikely at this size, but we will confirm once values are in.\n\nAssets she knows about:\n  - Home at 2207 Lakewood Terrace, Two Harbors, MN 55616. County\n    estimated market value $412,300. No mortgage.\n  - Cabin and 40 acres on Stewart Lake, held in the trust since 2011. This is\n    the only parcel with the old Halvorsen sawmill on it; Lars wants it.\n  - North Shore Federal Credit Union checking, acct ending 8841, about\n    $38,000, and a share certificate, $75,000.00, matures 09/15/2026.\n    NSFCU routing 047096417.\n  - Brokerage at Pinecrest Wealth Partners, acct PWP-7730-22914, roughly\n    $1.1 million at date of death. Adviser is Chase Whitlow\n    (cwhitlow@pinecrestwealth.example, 218.555.0116). Chase says step-up\n    statements will take two weeks.\n  - An old account in Cork from when Arvid worked there in the 1980s:\n    Gaelic Mutual Bank, IBAN IE10 AIBK 0892 6394 9967 82, maybe EUR 9,400.\n    Nobody has touched it in years.\n  - 2018 pickup, plate HLV 419, and a 19-ft aluminum boat, the \"Birgit II\".\n\nBeneficiaries under Article VI: Ingrid and her brother Lars Halvorsen, equal\nshares, after specific gifts: $25,000 to Bethel Lutheran Church and\nten thousand dollars to his caregiver, Soledad Marín. Ingrid mentioned that\nLars filed Chapter 13 in 2023 and is in recovery from a gambling addiction;\nshe asked whether his share can be held back. Told her the trust has a spendthrift\nclause but no discretionary holdback; see Minn. Stat. § 501C.0813 on her duty to\ninform. She is not to favor either beneficiary. The Crummey language is moot now.\n\n4/24/2026 (DV) -- Called NSFCU, spoke with \"Tammi\" in member services\n(1-800-555-0177 x4402). They need letters of trusteeship + death cert. to retitle.\nEmailed Ingrid at ingrid.hp@lakemail.example the certification of trust for signature.\nHer cell is (218) 555-0142; she is in Grand Marais Mon-Thu.\n\n4/29/2026 (RC) -- Lars called, upset. Says Ms. Marín \"got Dad to change things\" in\nthe last month at hospice and that Dad had vascular dementia since at least 2024.\nI told him we represent the trustee, not him, and that he may want his own lawyer.\nHe gave his number as 218 555 0190 and said to stop emailing his sister\nabout \"his\" cabin. Note to file: the gift to Ms. Marín was added by the Third\nAmendment dated January 12, 2026, four weeks before death. Need the\nhospice chart and the notary's journal. Possible capacity issue; flag for Renee.\n\nTO DO: EIN application; inventory within 60 days; Schedule K-1s at year end;\nask Whitlow for date-of-death values; retainer $5,000 received 4/23/2026, trust\nacct ref. IOLTA-22-0457.", "kind": "Text file", "detail": "541 words", "notes": [], "names": {"people": ["Ingrid Halvorsen-Pike", "Renee Castellano", "Dmitri Volkov", "Lars", "Chase Whitlow", "Ingrid", "Lars Halvorsen", "Soledad Marín", "Tammi", "Renee", "Whitlow"], "companies": ["CASTELLANO & BRIGHT LLP", "North Shore Federal Credit Union", "Pinecrest Wealth Partners", "Gaelic Mutual Bank", "AIBK", "Bethel Lutheran Church", "NSFCU"]}, "chunks": 2, "chunkErrors": 0, "importMs": 0.19999999925494194, "modelMs": 34004.199999999255, "detectors": ["email", "url", "ip", "iban", "card", "card_exp", "cvv", "ssn", "bn_ca", "sin_ca", "ein", "phone", "dob", "age90", "date", "passport_dl", "routing", "credential", "device", "vin", "record", "account", "money", "street", "zip", "postal_ca", "places", "names"], "detections": [{"start": 0, "end": 23, "text": "CASTELLANO & BRIGHT LLP", "kind": "company", "source": "short-form", "canonical": "CASTELLANO & BRIGHT LLP"}, {"start": 67, "end": 99, "text": "Halvorsen Family Revocable Trust", "kind": "company", "source": "short-form", "canonical": "Halvorsen Family Revocable Trust"}, {"start": 106, "end": 118, "text": "June 3, 2009", "kind": "date", "source": "pattern", "canonical": "June 3, 2009"}, {"start": 128, "end": 140, "text": "TR-2026-0318", "kind": "record", "source": "pattern", "canonical": "TR-2026-0318"}, {"start": 152, "end": 168, "text": "Renee Castellano", "kind": "person", "source": "model", "canonical": "Renee Castellano"}, {"start": 182, "end": 195, "text": "Dmitri Volkov", "kind": "person", "source": "model", "canonical": "Dmitri Volkov"}, {"start": 197, "end": 206, "text": "4/22/2026", "kind": "date", "source": "pattern", "canonical": "4/22/2026"}, {"start": 208, "end": 210, "text": "RC", "kind": "person", "source": "short-form", "canonical": "Renee Castellano"}, {"start": 250, "end": 271, "text": "Ingrid Halvorsen-Pike", "kind": "person", "source": "model", "canonical": "Ingrid Halvorsen-Pike"}, {"start": 312, "end": 330, "text": "Arvid T. Halvorsen", "kind": "person", "source": "short-form", "canonical": "Arvid T. Halvorsen"}, {"start": 336, "end": 352, "text": "February 9, 2026", "kind": "date", "source": "pattern", "canonical": "February 9, 2026"}, {"start": 356, "end": 375, "text": "Mercy Ridge Hospice", "kind": "company", "source": "short-form", "canonical": "Mercy Ridge Hospice"}, {"start": 394, "end": 400, "text": "age 94", "kind": "age90", "source": "pattern", "canonical": "age 94"}, {"start": 438, "end": 448, "text": "11/30/2019", "kind": "date", "source": "pattern", "canonical": "11/30/2019"}, {"start": 451, "